\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone 
\par 1. \i Land of our Birth, we pledge to thee
\par Our love and toil in the years to be;
\par When we are grown and take our place
\par As men and women with our race.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\i0\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone 
\par \pard\qj 2. Father in heaven, who lovest all,
\par O help Thy children when they call;
\par That they may build from age to age,
\par An undefiled heritage.
\par 
\par \pard\cf1\ul\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone 
\par \pard\qj 3. Teach us to bear the yoke in youth,
\par With steadfastness and careful truth;
\par That, in our time, Thy grace may give
\par The truth where the nations live.
\par 
\par \pard\cf1\ul\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone 
\par \pard\qj 4. Teach us to rule ourselves alway,
\par Controlled and cleanly night and day;
\par That we may bring, if need arise,
\par No mamed or worthless sacrifice.
\par 
\par \pard\cf1\ul\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone 
\par \pard\qj 5. Teach us to look, in all our ends,
\par On Thee for Judge, and not our friends;
\par That we, with Thee, may walk uncowed
\par By fear or favour of the crowd.
\par 
\par \pard\cf1\ul\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone 
\par \pard\qj 6. Teach us the strength that cannot seek,
\par By deed or thought, to hurt the weak;
\par That, under Thee, we may possess
\par Man's strength to succour man's distress.
\par 
\par \pard\cf1\ul\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone 
\par \pard\qj 7. Teach us delight in simple things,
\par And mirth that has no bitter springs;
\par Forgiveness free of evil done,
\par And love to all men 'neath the sun!
\par 
\par \pard\cf1\ul\'b6 Verse 8\cf0\ulnone 
\par \pard\qj 8. \i Land of our Birth, our faith, our pride,
\par For whose dear sake our fathers died;
\par O Motherland, we pledge to thee,
\par Head, heart, and hand through the years to be.\f1 
\par \pard\cf1\ul\i0 
\par }

